<title>BRAZIL: Brazil coffee coops report mild early temperatures.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee coops report mild early temperatures.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian cooperatives and weather monitoring centers in key coffee areas reported early morning temperatures of either 10 degrees Celsius or above on Thursday.</p>
<p>Weather services are expecting cool temperatures in the coffee areas over the coming days but no frosts are forecast.</p>
<p>Early morning/minimum temperatures were as follows.</p>
<p>PARANA, Londrina - 10 degrees Celsius</p>
<p>PARANA, Cornelio Procopio - 14 degrees Celsius</p>
<p>SAO PAULO, Marilia - 16 degrees Celsius</p>
<p>SAO PAULO, Franca - 18 degrees Celsius</p>
<p>MINAS GERAIS, Sao Sebastiao do Paraiso - 15 degrees Celsius</p>
<p>MINAS GERAIS, Pocos de Caldas - 13 degrees Celsius</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
